   "id": "syn-pltr-1",
   "text": "Palantir Technologies raised its revenue forecast for the year on Monday after a quarter in which its US commercial business grew faster than expected, driven by customers adopting its artificial intelligence platform.\n\nThe company reported quarterly revenue above analysts' estimates and its largest ever operating profit. The number of US commercial customers rose sharply from a year earlier, and government revenue also grew, helped by new defence contracts.\n\nThe chief executive said demand for the AI platform was unprecedented and that the company was adding sales capacity to keep up. Palantir expects to remain profitable on an adjusted basis every quarter this year.\n\nShares jumped in extended trading. Some analysts said the valuation of Palantir already assumes years of rapid growth, and that the stock's rise leaves little room for a slowdown.",
